{
  "version": "attribute-policy-v3",
  "instructions": [
    "Treat each module independently: an ambiguous shape must not erase a clearly shared function.",
    "Classification is a strict tree with exactly one domain root (organism, artifact, food, nature, abstract, fictional). Pick the most specific applicable leaf; parents are added locally. Harvested fruit and vegetables are food, never organism.",
    "Shape lists what a typical monochrome sketch shows: outline, visible parts and surface marks. Prefer the shared reusable tags. Usually 2-5 shape tags.",
    "Anatomy tags (ears, tails, whiskers, mane, horns, beak, fins, tentacles, feelers, pincers, long_snout) are literal and only for organisms, fictional beings and animal-shaped toys. Use handle, strap, loop, spout or tube tags for object parts.",
    "Function is the typical use for artifacts and the typical behavior for organisms. For natural things record only an observable action: lighting/heating (sun, fire), water_flow (river), precipitation (cloud, rain, snow), air_movement (storms), electric_power (lightning). Otherwise use not_applicable. Never invent a human purpose for nature.",
    "eating means an edible item, never a utensil, vessel, mouth or an animal's feeding. Use dining for cutlery, chewing for mouth/teeth, grazing/hunting/foraging for animals.",
    "Sensory body parts use seeing, hearing and smelling_breathing; tools that aid a sense may share the tag (eyeglasses seeing, stethoscope hearing, snorkel smelling_breathing).",
    "Do not force unique profiles. coffee_cup, cup and mug may overlap. Record genuine overlap in notes; never add the category name as a tag.",
    "For a polysemous label follow the catalog Korean name and the typical Quick Draw sample, and keep a short note about the other sense.",
    "uncertain is reserved for material ambiguity or a genuinely missing vocabulary term; explain the missing concept in a short note.",
    "Return a compact JSON object only. No duplicate tags. At most 12 tags per module including parents."
  ],
